  "note": "Its job is to let the term (5c₀c₂/3π²)D' log(√e x/D') from (4.47) be absorbed by −(2√(c₀c₁)/π)R log(ex/R) from (4.48), or by (2√(c₀c₁)/π)D log(ex/D) when D ≤ R. Lean uses c₂_identity in norm_restPartL_le_caseB (hB2, TypeILogProof.lean:1106; then hcancel) and in the proofs of Lemmas 4.2.2 and 4.2.4."
